WEBVTT

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.150
We need to become the MVPs.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.900
We're stopping the Quest 
Dorm from getting shut down,

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:13.860
and Souta from getting expelled!

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.780
Yeah!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.500
Yeah.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:28.340
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.000
<b>Flag 4</b>

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.000
<b>We're Almost to the Goal. The Track Meet'll End Just Fine.</b>

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:56.310
So this might be a bit late,

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.540
but what do we need 
to do to become MVPs?

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:00.180
Well, of course,

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.010
we need to get a high total score,

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:04.600
but the score's not the only thing.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.800
There's a lot of emphasis 
placed on special points

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.460
you can get for teamwork.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.750
So basically, whoever stands 
out the most, wins.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.160
Anyway, I've chosen which games you

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:17.860
should be able to get the most points in.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:18.680
Huh?

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.780
We're doing all these?!

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.120
<b>Sports Week</b>

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.120
<b>Daytime</b>

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.120
<b>Monday</b>

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.120
<b>Tuesday</b>

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.500
This does go on for a whole week.

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.790
A proper schedule is the key to victory.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.370
Looks like it's time for me to go already.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.610
I have the 100 meter preliminaries right now.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.700
The women's preliminaries 
are still a while off.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.970
<b>Ta-da</b>

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.600
<i>It's time for our special Sports Week 
program, </i>If I Don't do It, Who Will?

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.170
<i>I'll be your host, Seiteikouji Mimori!</i>

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:48.560
<i>My guest here is Hatagaya Academy's own 
walking dictionary, Ryuukishibara Tsumugi!</i>

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:49.310
<i>Hi.</i>

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:51.220
<i>When I was young, 
I was the anchor for a bucket relay</i>

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.770
<i>when the town was on fire.</i>

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.170
<i>Our program will pick up 
any news-worthy events</i>

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.030
<i>that happen around the clock.</i>

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.910
<i>First we had Hatagaya Academy's 
first martial arts tournament!</i>

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.590
<i>Surrounded by tough competitors, 
only one could stand on top!</i>

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.030
<i>And Eiyuuzaki Rin-kun was that woman!</i>

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:12.540
<i>I'm not sure you'd see that at a track meet...</i>

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.670
<i>Next we had the heavyweight 
cat-gathering competition!</i>

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.000
<i>The android everyone's talking 
about, Ninjabayashi Ruri-kun,</i>

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.110
<i>used the speaker in her mouth to broadcast 
a sound which only cats could hear,</i>

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.450
<i>and gathered them all up.</i>

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:27.260
<i>I don't even know what this 
is supposed to be now.</i>

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.520
<i>And we had a teacher massage contest!</i>

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.900
<i>This was just a throw-in for the teachers...</i>

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:35.310
<i>It's still the first day and 
we've hit the ground running!</i>

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.560
<i>The Quest Dorm team is 
really tearing it up.</i>

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.150
<i>Everyone cheer the Quest Dorm on!</i>

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.950
What's up with her?

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.890
I'm sure she feels responsible.

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.670
Oh, you did a good job, Nanami.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:53.750
You got first in the princess race.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.960
Oh, that...

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.030
Only real princesses can participate...

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.010
Why would there be an event like that?!

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.570
All right.

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:06.260
We're going to start our 
penalty shoot-out competition.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.510
What's a penalty shoot-out?

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:14.770
It's where you do soccer 
penalty kicks over and over.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.770
It's a contest that measures one's 
state of mind and composure.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:20.620
Can Souta really handle that?

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.780
Y-You can do it, Souta!

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.160
<i>The left!</i>

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:40.600
I see.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.480
This worked well for Souta.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.010
You were great, Souta!

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:48.110
You're moving on to the finals, Sou-kun!

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.490
Indeed. Good work, Souta.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:54.080
You're able to read people 
better than anyone.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.320
I'm sure you'll win tomorrow's 
finals just fine.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:02.150
Megu!

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:04.530
You just called for me, right?

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.440
Megu! They must have screwed up,

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.830
because they just announced 
you set a new course record!

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.450
I did just get a new record.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:13.450
Huh?

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.360
You guys didn't know?

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.250
She was constantly a contender in the

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.580
middle school championships 
for track-and-field.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:20.320
That's amazing, Megu-chan!

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.680
I didn't know you were 
in track-and-field!

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.940
Oh, I'm not in track-and-field anymore.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.050
What are you in, then?

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:29.830
The home ec club!

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.220
Totally should have expected that!

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:32.890
Gallop, gallop.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:35.460
Souta-kun!

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.990
Why are you on a horse?

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.730
I was just in a horse-riding 
competition.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:43.690
I won!

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.150
Wh-Why are you still riding?

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.910
I just kind of felt like it.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.680
What's your next event?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.740
I'll take you there.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.880
I-I'm fine.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:56.660
Looks kinda scary.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:58.710
Oh...

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.960
H-Hey.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:09.430
What's going on?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.650
For safety's sake, hold on tight!

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:15.230
Huh?

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:18.310
White King, hiyah!

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.230
You all did great out there today.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:25.650
We're currently in first place now.

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.280
However, we still have a long way to go.

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:31.310
Those that have night events 
will sleep after eating.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:32.740
I will not have anyone oversleeping.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.130
Night events... Early morning events...

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:38.500
That student council president 
never does anything right.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.590
But this is kinda fun.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.590
It kinda feels like we're 
on a club trip somewhere.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:47.450
It's always felt like we were 
all on a trip together.

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:49.730
I guess you could say we're having a

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.550
"strengthen our friendships" camp right now.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.140
Your poems are always so wonderful!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.520
Stop saying poem!

00:06:55.520 --> 00:06:57.200
I take that back!

00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:00.280
We've all become one to help you, Souta-kun.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.480
We really are strengthening our bonds!

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.770
Yeah, we're putting our friendships 
on the line to get that MVP spot!

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:09.190
I'm not really a friend, 
but an older sister,

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.450
so I'm not really becoming closer 
friends, but loving him even more.

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:15.740
All of you can love him more, if you'd like.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.330
Wh-What about you, Akane?

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.830
I think you get along with him best.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:25.670
What? I-I think that 
Megu-chan is best for him.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.820
N-No, it can't be me.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:31.720
I-I think Rin-senpai is best. 
She's known him since they were kids.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:32.940
Y-You think so?

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:34.510
No, I don't think...

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:37.550
<i>They're all trying to 
hand him to each other...</i>

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.460
We've decided to leave the love part to you,

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.740
Nanami-chan, through process of elimination.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.900
Now you're just pushing it on me!

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.270
I'm not going to let this go!

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:10.170
Living like this is spoiling me, 
and it's causing me to forget everything...

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.380
I...

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:17.720
<i>Time for the shoot out finals!</i>

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.980
<i>If he stops this shot, 
the Quest Dorm team wins!</i>

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.800
Souta-kun, we're here with you!

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.850
You can do it! 
Stop it with sheer willpower!

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:31.120
Oh, crap!

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:38.160
<i>Goal!</i>

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.860
<i>The handicraft team wins!</i>

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.390
We're currently in eighth place.

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:04.610
The last day is tomorrow...

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.480
I didn't think we'd have such a hard time.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.780
The men's teams are coming after us,

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.190
like they're getting revenge 
for their little brothers.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.320
I wonder why.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.710
I kind of understand.

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:17.320
Don't worry.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:21.080
We're going to save Souta-kun's Quest Dorm.

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.660
Yeah.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.340
Souta-san.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:34.590
I am a machine whose 
purpose is to help humans.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:36.940
Ruri, what are you saying...

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:41.510
Akane-san and the others are 
experiencing a dip in their morale vectors.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.330
I have inferred that this is

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.760
strongly connected to the current decline

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:49.690
in your morale vector.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:54.850
It is fatal if someone's morale vector
drops below a certain point.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:58.150
My "pursuit of human happiness" program

00:09:58.150 --> 00:09:59.700
suggests that this issue be resolved.

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.440
You don't have to worry.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:04.170
The reason everything is 
like this will be over soon.

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:09.250
Is that because you've 
resolved yourself to defeat?

00:10:13.210 --> 00:10:16.190
Ruri, let's talk where no one else is around.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:25.270
I'm...

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:30.310
going to die soon.

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:36.190
I cannot comprehend the concept of death.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:40.030
I am aware that humans instinctively

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:41.410
fear death, however.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:42.800
I'm scared of dying, of course,

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.570
but there's something 
I'm even more afraid of.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:48.120
When I die,

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.880
everyone else may feel 
sorrow because of that.

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:55.160
I'm going to make those that

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:56.800
care about me feel that way.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.160
I'm most afraid of that.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.970
If I leave the school on my own,

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:04.910
then the wounds I inflict 
will be much less deep.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.990
I want to clean things up after I leave.

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:11.110
Is there no way to avoid your death?

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:11.980
No.

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:17.180
I understood how to destroy other people's 
death flags in an instant,

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.540
but my own flag...

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:22.610
Oh, I know. That letter.

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:25.200
Princess knight,

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:26.740
magician,

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.710
bishop, ninja...

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.480
First Flag secret code: entry confirmed.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:39.500
White hacking mode released.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:40.790
Connecting directly to server.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:43.090
Direct access to kernel space granted.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.010
R-Ruri...

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:48.990
It seems you wish to proceed 
to the "shadows" of this world.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.720
Do you wish to make any corrections?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.270
Yes or no?

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:55.270
The "shadows" of this world?

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:58.250
The first gate that will be 
opened by the four heroes that

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.190
fly the Royal Banner is connected to

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.710
the "shadows" of this world.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.840
There waits one will destroy the

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:08.080
flag of death that eats 
away at the Royal Banner.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:11.110
The flag of death? Will destroy it?

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:14.080
So does that mean I can get 
rid of this death flag?

00:12:14.950 --> 00:12:17.800
But... who...

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.880
Have you heard of a girl named Sakura?

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:29.390
I do contain some data 
of a word close that one,

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.870
however I am unable to 
learn more at this time.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:33.490
I see...

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.940
Then do you know where 
this "first gate" is?

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.810
Searching for a readable cluster.

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.940
Would you like to project the program?

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:45.200
Yes or no.

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:46.730
Please do.

00:12:54.020 --> 00:12:56.450
This is the Quest Dorm?

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.940
What's wrong, Souta?

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:00.840
Huh? Nanami?

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.880
Don't just stand there.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:05.830
You are the Royal Banner.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:06.520
Huh?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.780
Akane, and Ruri, too...

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:13.930
So this person is the bishop?

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:16.370
Let's get going.

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.430
Right.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:30.420
Where are we going?

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.880
This is most likely the first gate.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:50.660
I will give you my power.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.910
And in exchange, you must

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:58.150
learn the ultimate truth of this world.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.280
That was...

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:03.830
Last updated: 1938.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:06.700
The record was created 
by Ninjabayashi Ruri.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:09.530
Ruri, you've been around that long?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.930
No, I began test operations

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.390
two months ago.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:16.710
I must assume it was 
someone by the same name.

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:19.000
Then was there anyone 
at Hatagaya Academy

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.620
with a word meaning 
"bishop" in their name?

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:24.610
Searching database.

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:28.470
Zero results.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:31.290
We don't know where this data came 
from, or even if it can be trusted.

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:32.330
But

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:34.960
if that door really does exist...

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:38.160
Then I can't leave Quest Dorm.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:40.480
The ultimate truth of this world...

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:44.250
If I can reach it, then I won't die.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.420
The others might not have to suffer.

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:50.910
Ruri, I need you.

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:53.050
I want you to help me.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:56.590
You need... me?

00:14:57.610 --> 00:15:01.070
There have been plenty of 
people who tolerated me.

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.420
But for someone to say they needed me?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:07.170
Hatate Souta-san, you're the first.

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:20.940
<i>This is the last day for Sports Week!</i>

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.940
<i>The last event is an obstacle 
relay race around the school!</i>

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:27.210
<i>If you manage to use your teamwork to</i>

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:29.990
<i>get around the various obstacles 
laid out in this large course,</i>

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:33.200
<i>you might be able to get MVP 
from an underdog position!</i>

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:35.510
So if we win, we're MVPs.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.110
That makes things easy.

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:38.840
I wonder if this'll work...

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.780
The final runners have to

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:43.460
run in pairs like this.

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:44.620
It's fine.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.920
The victory flags've been raised.

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:49.370
On your marks...

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:50.420
Ready...

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:55.550
<i>Souta-kun...</i>

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:58.030
What's wrong?

00:15:58.030 --> 00:15:59.280
Akane...

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.600
Please win.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:05.790
Do you think that I wouldn't try?

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:06.760
Thank you.

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:09.080
I'll have to make it up to you.

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:11.140
Oh, then could I ask something of you?

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:12.610
Sure. Anything's fine.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:15.620
Th-Then it's a promise.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:17.660
Pop.

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:19.490
It's a promise.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:21.160
Kikuno-senpai!

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:22.620
Okiku-nee,

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.090
I'm sorry for making 
you worry all the time,

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.920
and being such a terrible 
little brother character,

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.000
but I want you to win.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:29.590
You're not a little brother character.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.600
You're my little brother.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:34.780
Pop.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:38.350
<i>Older sisters are invincible when 
it comes to their little brothers.</i>

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:39.810
Megu-chan!

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:41.460
Megumu...

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:43.310
I'm not sure how to say this, but...

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:45.830
Is this...

00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.110
I understand... I understand, Souta-kun!

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.610
Pop, pop, pop, pop, pop!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.610
<i>Men don't need words to promise 
something to each other.</i>

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.910
Rin-senpai!

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:58.910
Rin-kun, thank you for 
trying so hard for me.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:00.660
I'm truly grateful to you.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.460
N-No problem.

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.970
I've always been best friends with you.

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:07.960
Yes.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:12.000
You could never be replaced in my heart—

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:13.340
you were my hero.

00:17:13.340 --> 00:17:14.730
Souta...

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:16.490
Pop, pop, pop, pop.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:19.910
So I want you to show me how 
cool you can be, once again.

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.140
<i>Just you wait, Souta!</i>

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:25.840
I see.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:29.820
I was wondering why you were 
running around all over the place.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:32.390
I was just using everyone.

00:17:32.870 --> 00:17:34.000
But still, I...

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:35.380
Ridiculous.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:38.820
They fall head over heels for you, 
and you're worried about that?

00:17:39.090 --> 00:17:42.380
By the way, I don't really 
care about this MVP stuff.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:44.580
I just don't like losing to others.

00:17:44.860 --> 00:17:45.930
Yeah.

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:49.320
I don't know how to get your victory 
flag up, even though I knew the others—

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:50.090
Huh?

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:54.840
<i>You know, I've never seen a flag of hers.</i>

00:17:55.340 --> 00:17:57.840
<i>Does Nanami not have flags?</i>

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:01.020
Souta!

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:02.220
Take it!

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:04.360
Let's go, Nanami!

00:18:04.360 --> 00:18:05.630
We're going to stay in the lead!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:07.600
Yeah, we're going to be MVPs!

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:14.210
We're almost there!

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.150
I know!

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.260
Fight!

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:20.290
You can do it!

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:21.600
Show us what you're made of!

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.660
You're almost there!

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:26.010
<i>Quest Dorm team is in first!</i>

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.680
<i>All they have to do is put 
their ice on the table,</i>

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:29.970
<i>and run to the goal!</i>

00:18:29.970 --> 00:18:30.670
All right. Let's go.

00:18:35.100 --> 00:18:36.720
Nanami, are you okay?!

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:40.510
Just a small scrape.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:42.170
Don't push yourself.

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:43.170
We can go to the infirmary.

00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:45.970
No, there's only half a lap left.

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:46.950
Let's go.

00:18:48.050 --> 00:18:50.000
Why are we the anchors if we can't deliver the sash,

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.300
containing everyone's feelings, 
to the finish line properly?

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:55.070
Fine. Let's go, Nanami.

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.820
Yeah, it's the last spurt!

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:02.070
You can do it!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.360
I'm sorry, Souta...

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:10.800
No, you saved me from...

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.580
Not that...

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.590
If I had a victory flag, too...

00:19:16.070 --> 00:19:16.840
Nanami...

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:18.880
<i>Will I</i>

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:22.140
<i>only bring sorrow to everyone?</i>

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.820
<i>Is it right for me to just disappear?</i>

00:19:27.650 --> 00:19:28.800
I'm sorry, Nanami.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:31.310
Let's go.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.320
<i>But I still want to be...</i>

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:39.070
<i>...with everyone...</i>

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:42.930
<i>...there at Quest Dorm...</i>

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.330
I want to be with everyone!

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:49.330
<i>Quest Dorm team is catching 
up at a crazy pace!</i>

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:54.310
Go!

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:58.300
<i>Who got to the finish line first?!</i>

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:01.800
Quest Dorm Team 

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:01.800
<b>Hatagaya Academy 
Around the school obstacle relay</b>

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:05.390
<b>Photo finish</b>

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:00.250
<i>Photo finish.</i>

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:01.720
<i>First is...</i>

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:05.390
<b>1st Place: Baseball Team</b>

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:05.390
<b>2nd Place: Quest Dorm Team</b>

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:05.390
<i>First is the baseball team!</i>

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:08.140
<i>The Quest Dorm team is a close second.</i>

00:20:08.610 --> 00:20:12.060
So what does this mean...

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:13.980
We lost.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.450
Does that mean Souta-kun is going to...

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:16.730
That can't be...

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.020
Thank you, everyone.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:24.240
I'm really glad I got to work so hard 
towards something with all of you.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:25.780
I'm at fault here.

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.660
If I hadn't been hurt...

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:30.080
Souta-kun...

00:20:32.390 --> 00:20:33.030
Huh?

00:20:33.030 --> 00:20:35.170
We were moved!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:39.300
These are the people on the board 
that were complaining about you.

00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:43.130
You had an accident, and you still 
carried your friend to the finish line.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:45.170
You believed in your friends 
to the last minute,

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:47.920
and called out to them, cheering them on.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:51.000
This is true friendship, true teamwork.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:54.610
But it doesn't change the fact that 
Souta will be kicked out of the dorm!

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:57.250
Second place and better are pretty 
much guaranteed to get MVP.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:58.170
Huh?

00:20:58.170 --> 00:20:59.360
So that means...

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:01.400
Quest Dorm gets to stay?

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:03.200
Yay!

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:10.350
I guess I was wrong.

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:11.950
You again?!

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.590
Hatate Souta...

00:21:24.870 --> 00:21:27.300
I see. So he's the one...

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:12.310
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:14.320
The athletic festival's finally over.

00:23:14.320 --> 00:23:16.940
At least, that's what everyone thought...

00:23:16.940 --> 00:23:18.750
Don't set up a continuation flag!

00:23:18.750 --> 00:23:20.550
Ignoring Mimori's nonsense,

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:23.510
what are you planning to do for break 
now that the festival's over, Nanami?

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:26.240
Well, I've been busy lately,

00:23:26.240 --> 00:23:27.890
so I've been thinking 
of relaxing at the dorm.

00:23:27.890 --> 00:23:30.610
At least, that's what everyone thought...

00:23:30.610 --> 00:23:32.370
Don't keep setting up these flags!

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:34.930
<b>Flag 5</b>

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:34.930
<b>Believe and Wait for Me. 
I'm not Going to be Late for My Date With Everyone.</b>

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:33.880
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>I hope you watch us next time!</b>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Illustration: Hikawa Hekiru
